<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Tordenskjold</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1690–1720</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Peter Wessel Tordenskiold</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Tordenskjold, born Peter Wessel in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trondheim">Trondheim</a>, was a Norwegian-born naval officer in the service of Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>. Ennobled in 1716, he won fame through bold actions such as the destruction of a Swedish transport fleet at Dynekilen in 1716 and the capture of Marstrand in 1719. He was killed in a duel in 1720.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-tordenskjold.jpg" alt="Peter Tordenskjold" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Balthasar Denner · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viseadmiral_Peter_Wessel_Tordenskjold_(1690_-_1720)_(3610418617).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
